abstract: >-
  This evidence-backed personal investigation examines whether intuition can be useful as an early anomaly-detection signal without being treated as evidence of causation. A retrospectively reported period of fatigue, sleepiness, muscular weakness, reduced exercise capacity, and reduced ability to sustain deep work was reconstructed using Mac and iPhone behavioral traces and compared with selected space-weather observations. The record contains both temporal coincidence and important counterexamples. In particular, geomagnetically active intervals on August 18–19 occurred alongside comparatively high Mac activity, weakening a simple model in which geomagnetic activity alone is sufficient to explain the later behavioral state. The paper therefore treats intuition as a hypothesis generator and distinguishes anomaly detection from causal identification. No causal biological effect of space weather is claimed.
